---
// Temporary preview for the track-colour decision (build-order gate 1.3).
// Renders representative course-page chrome under a live theme switcher.
// Never linked from anywhere; delete once track colours are chosen.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Theme preview" description="Track colour decision preview — all five ramps on one page.">

  <div class="course-page">
    <div class="course-content">

      <div class="theme-switcher" id="theme-switcher">
        <span class="theme-switcher__label">Theme</span>
        <button data-t="default" data-pair="F2 · Royal Blue × Spring Green" class="is-active">Blue Lagoon</button>
        <button data-t="green" data-pair="F8 · Forest × Hot Pink">Canopy</button>
        <button data-t="purple" data-pair="F3 · Plum × Mint">Fusion</button>
        <button data-t="red" data-pair="F5 · Burgundy × Aqua">Ember</button>
        <button data-t="mono" data-pair="05 · Ink × Mint">Graphite</button>
        <span id="theme-pair" style="flex-basis:100%; font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:10px; color:var(--text-muted); letter-spacing:0.06em;">Pair: F2 · Royal Blue × Spring Green — <span style="display:inline-block; width:120px; height:10px; border-radius:3px; vertical-align:middle; background:var(--grad-pair);"></span></span>
      </div>

      <header class="course-header">
        <p class="course-header__day">M1 · Mathematical Foundations · ~70 min</p>
        <h1 class="course-header__title">Vectors as Meaning</h1>
        <p class="course-header__desc">What a vector is, what the dot product measures, and why cosine similarity — not distance — is how machines compare texts.</p>
        <p class="prereq-chips">
          <span class="prereq-chips__label">Requires</span>
          <a class="prereq-chip" href="#">Python Setup</a>
          <span class="prereq-chip prereq-chip--planned">Matrices as Maps <span class="planned-tag">planned</span></span>
        </p>
        <p class="course-header__notebook" style="margin-top:18px; display:flex; gap:18px; align-items:center; flex-wrap:wrap;">
          <a class="btn-primary" href="#">Play with this notebook in Colab <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
          <a class="btn-link-v3" href="#">View on GitHub <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="prose">

        <section class="opening-narrative">
          <p class="lead-paragraph">Every method in this curriculum — embeddings, attention, fine-tuning — begins with the same move: text becomes points in a space, and questions about meaning become questions about geometry.</p>
          <div class="key-takeaway">
            <p class="key-takeaway__label">After This Module You Will Be Able To</p>
            <ol>
              <li>Describe a vector geometrically and algebraically, and move between the two.</li>
              <li>Give all three readings of the dot product and say when each is the useful one.</li>
              <li>Explain why cosine similarity is used for text rather than Euclidean distance.</li>
            </ol>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>The Dot Product</h2>
          <p>The dot product has three readings, and their equivalence is this section's payload. A survey respondent is a vector of answers; two similar respondents are near each other. The geometry was always there — nobody drew it.</p>

          <div class="definition-box">
            <p class="definition-box__term">Cosine similarity</p>
            <p>The cosine of the angle between two vectors: direction without magnitude. A long document and a short one on the same topic should be similar — and cosine says they are.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="widget-wrap">
            <p class="widget-eyebrow">Interactive</p>
            <p class="widget-title">Vector Playground</p>
            <p class="widget-intro">Drag both vectors. Watch the dot product pass through zero as you rotate past perpendicular — then normalise, and watch it become exactly the cosine.</p>
            <div style="height:120px; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; border:1px dashed var(--border); border-radius:6px; color:var(--text-dim); font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:11px;">widget canvas</div>
          </div>

          <div class="key-takeaway">
            <p class="key-takeaway__label">Key Takeaway</p>
            <p>Positive means aligned, zero means orthogonal — <em>unrelated</em>, which is the reading that matters for embeddings — and negative means opposed.</p>
          </div>
        </section>

      </div>

    </div>
  </div>

  <style is:global>
    .theme-switcher {
      position: sticky;
      top: 70px;
      z-index: 50;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 6px;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      background: var(--elevated, #fff);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 8px;
      padding: 8px 12px;
      margin-bottom: 28px;
      box-shadow: 0 2px 12px rgba(0,0,0,0.06);
    }
    .theme-switcher__label {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 9px;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.14em;
      color: var(--text-muted);
      margin-right: 6px;
    }
    .theme-switcher button {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 11px;
      padding: 4px 12px;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 4px;
      background: var(--surface);
      color: var(--text-sec);
      cursor: pointer;
    }
    .theme-switcher button.is-active {
      border-color: var(--accent);
      color: var(--accent);
    }
  </style>

  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var sw = document.getElementById('theme-switcher');
      if (!sw) return;
      sw.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
        var b = e.target.closest('button[data-t]');
        if (!b) return;
        var t = b.getAttribute('data-t');
        if (t === 'default') document.documentElement.removeAttribute('data-theme');
        else document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', t);
        sw.querySelectorAll('button').forEach(function (x) { x.classList.toggle('is-active', x === b); });
        var pair = document.getElementById('theme-pair');
        if (pair) pair.firstChild.textContent = 'Pair: ' + b.getAttribute('data-pair') + ' — ';
      });
    })();
  </script>

</Base>
